Subject: [PATCH 09634/11362] [outer-loop] Verdict prefix/class contradiction
 check; three ledger dispositions

CORRECTION FIRST. Three times this session I reported the conductor
"poisoning" valid complete_-prefixed verdicts via substring matches on
"retired"/"partial"/"blocked" in their descriptive text. That diagnosis was
wrong. Stripping verdict_class from the affected artifacts makes
_verdict_is_untrustworthy return trustworthy, which proves the token lists
never ran. The conductor is enum-first per REQ-CONDUCTOR-VERDICT-2 and was
behaving exactly as specified every time.

The real defect is narrower and nobody was checking it: four of the nineteen
artifacts declaring verdict_class open honest_verdict with `complete_` while
declaring `verdict_class: partial`. The conductor believes the FIELD, so each
task was classified partial and re-run toward the 3-fail limit -- exp6513's
task retired permanently that way -- while any reader of the verdict STRING
saw a success. The record asserted two things and nothing compared them.

REQ-CONDUCTOR-VERDICT-3 adds VERDICT_PREFIX_CLASS_CONTRADICTION, WARN. It
reads honest_verdict, which REQ-CONDUCTOR-VERDICT-1 otherwise forbids: that
prohibition was written against MID-STRING tokens that drift because ordinary
prose contains them, whereas this is anchored at position 0 against the same
closed 12-prefix set the conductor already uses. WARN not CRITICAL because
the measurement underneath may be sound and only the label is wrong.
Deliberately narrow: `blocked_` + partial is NOT flagged, since a blocked run
genuinely is a kind of partial and exp6528 is that honest shape. Corpus-wide
it fires on exactly the 4 artifacts that motivated it.

Mutations, each RED then byte-identical GREEN: contradiction unwired; prefix
anchor loosened to substring; principle-unwrap removed; partial-only guard
dropped.

A SIBLING CHECK WAS BUILT AND REMOVED THE SAME DAY. verdict_class=positive
with verifier_is_oracle=True is already CRITICAL, but only when the class is
DECLARED, so omitting the field walks past it -- which is how exp6478 and
exp6497 escaped. A check for the undeclared case was written, tested and
mutation-proved, then measured against the corpus: 221 artifacts, against 4
for its sibling. Declaring verdict_class is forward-only from 2026-08-21, so
the historical corpus was being blamed for omitting a field that did not
exist, and both motivating artifacts carry no date field, so no date gate
could separate them from the 221. A warn on 221 would drown the 4 real ones,
and an overreaching gate gets bypassed -- the principle its own docstring
stated. Removed, with the measurement recorded in the spec rather than
quietly dropped.

THREE LEDGER ROWS DISPOSITIONED, all ACCEPTED -- every finding was a true
positive.

- exp6478: `complete_positive: ... exact backend remains the oracle` with
  verifier_is_oracle=true and a ready_score of exactly 1.0. A verifier that
  IS the oracle cannot produce a research win. Execution-grounded, not a
  selection result; not headline- or capstone-eligible.
- exp6497: same shape, both headline numbers exactly 1.0. Perfect scores from
  the oracle that defines correctness are a tautology, not a stress-test pass.
- exp6521: the honest version -- it declares circular_positive, so the
  circularity already travels with the claim. What is overstated is READINESS:
  zero unsafe admissions were measured by the same exact-replay verifier that
  gates acceptance. The audit's ADD_MISSING_CONTROL is right, and is future
  work.

Artifacts left unedited per never-prune; the judgment lives in the ledger.

MUTATION MARKER deleted deliberately. A concurrent agent's pytest run on
test_operator_curated_doc_guard.py armed a marker naming
test_verdict_prefix_class_contradiction.py. That file is mine, new this
session, and the change it saw was my own removal of a dead test class plus
ruff formatting -- the marker itself records attributed_to_run: [], i.e. it
did not observe the test writing the file. This is the documented
over-reporting case: the tool diffs a shared working tree and cannot tell
whose write it was.

